input.content:
// One-off: records the shotgun decisions in the GDD and the GLB analysis in the day entry. Run from C:\GameJam.
const fs = require('fs');
function edit(p, fn) {
  const raw = fs.readFileSync(p, 'utf8');
  const nl = raw.includes('\r\n') ? '\r\n' : '\n';
  let s = raw.split('\r\n').join('\n');
  s = fn(s, (a, b) => { if (!s.includes(a)) throw new Error('not found in ' + p + ': ' + a.slice(0, 60)); s = s.split(a).join(b); return s; });
  fs.writeFileSync(p, s.split('\n').join(nl));
}

edit('Design/GDD.md', (s, rep) => {
  s = rep('> Status: **v0.31, 2026-11-12**', '> Status: **v0.33, 2026-11-12**');
  s = rep('## Changelog\n', '## Changelog\n- v0.33 (2026-11-12): owner, on the shotgun: it loads **shell by shell** (not a magazine swap), and its **forend pumps** after every shot. Its model is a Tripo science-fiction shotgun. Rules and the architect\'s provisional numbers in §18 "Reload".\n');
  s = rep('Ammo pickups give one spare magazine, up to the gun\'s maximum.\n',
    'Ammo pickups give one spare magazine, up to the gun\'s maximum.\n' +
    '  - **The shotgun loads shell by shell (owner, 2026-11-12).** One shell goes in at a time; nothing is lost by reloading early, and the reload can stop part-way. Provisional (architect): its reserve is counted in shells (4 magazines x 6 = 24, the same total as before); each shell takes `ReloadTime / MagazineSize` (0.33 s), so a full reload from empty still takes the 2 s the balance tables use and Rapid Reload speeds it the same way; pressing fire during the reload stops it and shoots as soon as a shell is in (the shell on its way in is not lost: it stays in the reserve); an ammo pickup gives one magazine\'s worth of shells (6); an empty shotgun still starts reloading by itself.\n' +
    '  - **The shotgun\'s forend pumps after every shot (owner, 2026-11-12).** Provisional (architect): it is only the look; the time between shots stays `FireInterval` (0.8 s) and the pump plays inside it.\n');
  return s;
});

edit('Devlog/days/2026-11-12.md', (s, rep) => {
  s = rep('**Not imported into Unreal.** The source sits in `Glyphbound/SourceArt/Weapons/Shotgun/` (outside git, README tracked).\n- **Implementer exception:** done by the architect directly, not Muse Spark: reading renders and deciding on them.\n',
`**The owner's three answers** (one question dialog, three parts):
- Source: "La reexporto" ("I will re-export it").
- Reload: "Cartucho a cartucho" ("shell by shell"), against the architect's recommendation of the cheaper cell swap. It changes the ammunition logic (a reserve counted in shells, a reload that can stop part-way) and needs its own animation. Recorded in the GDD, v0.33, with the architect's provisional numbers: 0.33 s per shell, so a full reload still takes the 2 s the balance tables use.
- Pump: yes.

**The re-export arrives: \`futuristic rifle 3d model.glb\`.** Owner (translated): "I'd like you to pay special attention to the cables; analyse the texture well." Original: "Quisiera que le prestaras especial atencion a los cables, analiza bien la textura."
