  let s = get();
  const i = s.indexOf('  - the cell: a cylinder of dim glass');
  const j = s.indexOf('\n', i);
  s = s.slice(0, i) +
    "  - the cell: the GLB's own lumpy cell is deleted (949 faces) and a canister sits in its bay on the same axis: a metal collar at each end sunk into the bay's leaning walls, a glass body 25.8 mm in radius that glows evenly, two metal bands, four guard rods, a saddle up to the barrel and a foot under each band;" +
    s.slice(j);
  set(s);
  rep('- **Textures** (4096, packed in the file)', "- **Side plates:** the slab on each side of the receiver carried a painted data screen. Its face (102 × 65 mm, tilted 9° to 11°) is redrawn by position: an engraved border, a bolt in each corner, an abstract sigil inlaid with the glow (a diamond, a smaller one inside, a bar on each side) and three slanted slots.\n- **Textures** (4096, packed in the file)");
  rep('`Shotgun_Body` (31,413 triangles', '`Shotgun_Body` (31,536 triangles');
  rep("`Devlog/media/2026-11-12/17a…17u_shotgun_*.png`", "`Devlog/media/2026-11-12/17a…17z_shotgun_*.png`");
  rep("the screens' glyphs are the source's invented signs, re-cut;", "the small panel on the left of the receiver, near the stock, still shows one of the source's invented signs;");
});

edit('Devlog/days/2026-11-12.md', (rep) => {
  rep('## Design decisions\n', `## Thirtieth block: the owner's notes on the shotgun: the cell and the side screens
The owner sent a crop of the render with the cell and the side screen and two notes (translated): "Give this part another go. Analyse it; I think it lacks form, it looks odd. It looks a bit out of place there, and crooked." and "Remove that data panel on the side that simulates a screen; put some design or something that is not electronic."

**The cell, analysed with measurements before changing it.** The build script got a stage that prints the bay around the cell as tables of ray-cast hits (from both sides, from below, and looking at each wall from inside the bay). They explained all three complaints:
- **Out of place:** the modelled cylinder had been made fatter (radius 32.7 mm, to cover the GLB's lumps under it) than the bay it sits in, so it cut into the parts around it.
- **Crooked:** the bay's two walls are not square to the barrel. The forend's rear wall leans 14° and the receiver's front wall 20.5°. A cylinder with square ends met them at a slant, with ragged ends.
- **No form:** it was a plain tube with three stripes: no ends, no seat, nothing holding it.
- A fourth thing the tables showed: this part of the gun is not centred on the bounding box. Its left faces are at +44.5 mm and its right ones at -39.1, so its centre line is at +2.7 mm; the fitted axis (+2.4) was right.

**The new cell** (\`17v_shotgun_cell_canister.png\`, \`17w_shotgun_cell_side.png\`):
- The GLB's own cell is deleted, 949 faces: those near the fitted axis that face away from it, plus its leftovers in the bay. The barrel's underside and the walls face the axis and stay.
- A canister takes its place on the same axis: a metal collar at each end, long enough to sink into its leaning wall; a thinner glass body (25.8 mm) that glows evenly; two metal bands; four guard rods from collar to collar.
- With the old cell gone, the background showed through between the canister and the barrel. A saddle now joins it to the barrel's underside, and a foot under each band stands on the keel.
- The glass glows less (mask 0.36) over a dark teal, so the lights still shade it round. At 0.50 it rendered as a flat cyan shape.
- 2,224 triangles.

**The side screens become plates** (\`17x_shotgun_side_plate.png\`, \`17y_shotgun_side_plate_right.png\`). The slab's geometry stays; its face is redrawn in the texture by where each texel is on the plate. The script finds the face (the texels on the slab's plane), fits its long axis (102 × 65 mm, tilted 9° on the left and 11° on the right), and draws in that frame:
- an engraved border and a slotted bolt in each corner;
- an abstract sigil inlaid with the glow: a diamond, a smaller one inside, a bar on each side. It is not electronic and it is the gun's only mark; in the game it will take the enchant's colour like every glow. No real sign or letter was used;
- three slanted slots.
- The engraving goes into the normal map like every drawn detail.

**A mistake of the session:** one edit of the build script replaced "from the cell's function to the next section" and took the helper functions of every modelled part with it. The run failed at once on a missing name; the block was restored from the last commit.

**Left as it was:** the small panel on the left of the receiver, near the stock, still shows one of the source's invented signs. The owner was told.
- \`Shotgun.blend\` rebuilt and replaced in \`SourceArt\`. Still not imported.
- **Implementer exception:** done by the architect directly, not Muse Spark: reading renders and deciding on them.

## Design decisions
`);
  rep("the loading port with a shell on its way out, the pump at the back of its travel, and the rear three-quarters.\n",
      "the loading port with a shell on its way out, the pump at the back of its travel, and the rear three-quarters.\n" +
      "- `media/2026-11-12/17v_shotgun_cell_canister.png`, `17w_shotgun_cell_side.png`, `17x_shotgun_side_plate.png`, `17y_shotgun_side_plate_right.png`, `17z_shotgun_notes_first_person.png` (thirtieth block; Blender Cycles renders, not the game): after the owner's notes: the cell as a canister in its bay (the owner's own view of it, and from the side), the left and right side plates that replace the screens, and the player's camera.\n");
});
console.log('ok');

